# Tokoro OS: Acer mode-key remap.
#
# This file is intentionally empty of mappings. Run
#
#     sudo tokoro acer learn
#
# and press the Nitro key once. tokoro-acer-learn appends a mapping like
#
#     evdev:name:AT Translated Set 2 keyboard
#      KEYBOARD_KEY_ab=prog1
#
# then reloads systemd-hwdb and re-triggers input devices. Keeping the mapping
# out of the image avoids shipping a guessed scan code that could hijack a real
# key on a different Nitro V revision.
